; Forest — TerrainDefinition data entry (spec.md -> Data Schemas; terrain.md ->
; Already-Defined Terrain, v1 tag-source mapping).
;
; emitted_tags = ["forest"] is DECIDED (terrain.md's tag-source mapping, #5 closed ->
; D-25). Forest emits `forest` and NOT `cover`: rock is the v1 `cover` source, which is
; what keeps Fox habitat a two-brushstroke composition (forest NEAR rock) instead of a
; side effect of painting forest for Wood. Adding `cover` here would silently collapse
; that design.
;
; cost = 0 — nature is free (terrain.md), and here that rule is load-bearing rather than
; cosmetic: free Forest IS the no-dead-ends guarantee. A player at zero Wood can always
; paint Forest, wait, and build again.
;
; harvestable -> forest_harvest.tres. Forest is v1's sole harvestable.
;
; MODEL_SCENE NOW POINTS AT REAL ART: CommonTree1.tscn (CC0, MegaKit), chosen over
; CommonTree2 as the default because it is listed first among the two "common" picks
; documented in content-pipeline-status.md and no distinguishing reason favors the other;
; CommonTree2 remains imported and available at
; project/assets/terrain/common_tree_2/CommonTree2.tscn for a future per-tile variety pass
; (out of scope here — no random-variant scattering logic added). Scale is still the
; FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL recorded in CommonTree1.tscn's own header comment (raw mesh scaled
; to a ~2.5-tile canopy height, judgment call, no GDD number) — NOT eyeball-confirmed
; in-engine; that confirmation is a human call, not this repo's to make.
;
; SLAB REINSTATED (2026-08-03) in CommonTree1.tscn: TerrainView._refresh_tile_visual()
; instantiates model_scene as a tile's ENTIRE visual, and the trunk+canopy prop alone left
; much of the tile showing scenes/Main.tscn's configured WorldEnvironment sky-blue
; background_color (0.53, 0.72, 0.86) straight through the gap — reported by an in-engine
; human look as "a lot of transparency, lots of blue showing." Fixed by reinstating a
; ground slab matching the grey-box placeholder's geometry and color verbatim. See
; CommonTree1.tscn's own header for detail. Prop-on-slab look still awaits full human
; sign-off.
;
; MODEL_SCENE PLURALIZED TO MODEL_SCENES (-> D-42): the field is now an array so a
; terrain can carry multiple interchangeable visual variants, stably picked per tile by
; TerrainDefinition.pick_variant().
;
; LOOK-PASS REWORK (2026-08-16): CommonTree2 is now wired as a second live variant
; alongside CommonTree1 (equal weight, no ordering preference — both are "the common set"
; per art.md, and D-42's pick_variant() is a stable hash, not a priority list). CommonTree2
; was brought to visual parity with CommonTree1 first (slab + floor-blotch patches added —
; see CommonTree2.tscn's own header) so a tile does not visibly change floor treatment
; depending on which tree it lands. No new tree source was pulled in for this pass (the
; task's "1-2 more if a good candidate exists" was optional) — the 2 existing common trees
; already give real per-tile alternation, which is the D-42 capability this pass exists to
; exercise.
;
; blocks_movement = true, ADDED (animal-navigation pass, 2026-08-24): the trees Forest paints
; are now a real pathing obstacle for roaming animals — human-confirmed only Forest gets this
; in the first pass; Rock stays crossable (deferred, human's call to revisit).
;
; THIRD VARIANT ADDED (2026-08-16, human-reported follow-up, same day): human eyeball pass
; on the look-pass above reported "It does not seem like forest cycles between multiple
; assets." pick_variant()'s hash was confirmed still distributing evenly and both trees
; were confirmed correctly wired — the actual problem was that CommonTree1 and CommonTree2
; are both "common tree" picks from the same MegaKit set at the same ~2.5-tile canopy
; height, and read as visually indistinguishable at the fixed ~45 camera pitch. Added
; PineTree.tscn — a freshly-sourced, genuinely different silhouette (a narrow tapered
; conifer, not another round-canopy common tree; "Pine Tree" by Quaternius, CC0, sourced
; fresh via poly.pizza — see PineTree.tscn's own header and
; quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres) — as a third equal-weight model_scenes entry. Both
; existing trees are UNCHANGED and still live; this adds variety, it does not replace
; anything.
;
; 5 MORE VARIANTS ADDED (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 5), taking model_scenes from
; 3 to 8: BirchTree.tscn (Ultimate Nature Pack, CC0, thin trunk / light canopy, ~2.5-tile
; height), DeadTree.tscn (Textured Stylized Trees, CC0, bare-branch silhouette, ~2.2-tile —
; deliberately shorter than the living-canopy trees, see its own header), PineTree2.tscn
; (Textured Stylized Trees, CC0, a second conifer — same ~2.5-tile height as PineTree.tscn
; but a NON-UNIFORM scale for a deliberately narrower footprint, see its own header for
; why a plain uniform rescale couldn't hit both targets at once), Bush.tscn and
; BushBerries.tscn (both Ultimate Nature Pack, CC0, the first two non-tree, ground-level
; undergrowth picks, ~0.6-tile height, well under every tree). Quaternius CC0 for all 5,
; License.txt re-checked per-pack before import (asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate).
; Attribution: BirchTree/Bush/BushBerries extend the existing
; quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres assets_used list; DeadTree/PineTree2 are recorded in
; a newly-authored quaternius_textured_stylized_trees.tres (first use of that pack in this
; project). EVERY new scale is a FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number — FLAG FOR
; HUMAN SIGN-OFF on all 5 (per-scene headers carry the specific reasoning and open
; questions: DeadTree's shorter-height judgment call and bare-branch read, PineTree2's
; non-uniform-scale footprint squash, Bush/BushBerries' undergrowth-scale-class read and
; BushBerries' berry-detail legibility at scale). All 3 existing trees are UNCHANGED and
; still live; this adds variety, it does not replace anything. All 8 variants are equal
; weight in pick_variant() — no ordering/priority intended.
;
; 2 VARIANTS REMOVED (2026-09-08, human eyeball ruling), taking model_scenes from 8 back to
; 6: DeadTree.tscn and PineTree2.tscn are both UNWIRED. The ruling was explicit and was not
; about either asset's own quality — "Remove the Dead Tree" outright, and "The Pine Tree 2
; does not match the style of the other" — so this is a STYLE-CONSISTENCY cull, the same
; kind of call that culled Cactus/Palm out of wild_grass.tres. Both were the only two
; entries sourced from the Textured Stylized Trees pack, so that pack now contributes
; nothing to this terrain; quaternius_textured_stylized_trees.tres is left in place and its
; assets_used list is UNCHANGED, because the .tscn wrappers and their imported source files
; are still in the repo (unwired, not deleted — same disposition wild_grass.tres's
; WildGrassCactus/WildGrassPalm have). Do not re-add either without a fresh human ruling.
; The 6 survivors still span three packs and are NOT yet style-consistent with each other —
; the human has flagged that CommonTree1/CommonTree2 (Stylized Nature MegaKit, textured)
; and BirchTree/Bush/BushBerries (Ultimate Nature Pack, flat-shaded) "are not even close to
; being similar", with a single-pack standardisation pass still to come. This edit is only
; the removal half of that; it does not close the consistency question.
;
; PINETREE REMOVED TOO (2026-09-08, same human pass), 6 -> 5. This one is NOT a quality
; ruling either: PineTree.tscn is the project's only Poly Pizza-sourced tree, and the
; standardisation target has since been settled as the Stylized Nature MegaKit — the pack
; that already supplies the GROUND these trees stand on (grass.tres, meadow.tres,
; wild_grass.tres all draw from it), which is the adjacency that reads hardest. A one-off
; from a third pack cannot survive that, whatever it looks like on its own.
;
; KNOWN REGRESSION, ACCEPTED AND FLAGGED: PineTree was added on 2026-08-16 specifically to
; answer "every tree looks the same" — it was the only NARROW TAPERED CONIFER silhouette in
; the list, and the two CommonTrees are both round-canopy. Removing it costs that contrast
; until a MegaKit replacement lands. THE REPLACEMENT EXISTS AND IS IN THE ALREADY-AUDITED
; PACK: the MegaKit ships Pine_1..5 with their own Leaf_Pine/Leaf_Pine_C texture set, plus
; TwistedTree_1..5 (own Bark_TwistedTree/Leaves_TwistedTree set) as a THIRD, gnarled
; silhouette. Neither family is imported yet and neither has been eyeballed at the game's
; camera pitch, so the silhouette gap is RECOVERABLE, not closed — do not treat it as closed
; until a Pine is actually in and looked at.
;
; DO NOT CONFUSE MegaKit `Pine_*` WITH THE `PineTree2.tscn` REMOVED ABOVE. That one came from
; the Textured Stylized Trees pack, whose assets_used happens to record a "Pine_2" of its
; own — a different pack, a different mesh, different textures. Importing a MegaKit pine is
; new work, not a re-add of something this same pass just culled.
;
; The MegaKit has no BIRCH mesh at any name, so BirchTree.tscn has no like-for-like
; replacement in it; that swap (if it happens) is a substitution, not a port.
;
; The 5 survivors are still two packs: CommonTree1/CommonTree2 (MegaKit, matching the
; ground) and BirchTree/Bush/BushBerries (Ultimate Nature Pack, flat-shaded). The MegaKit
; replacements for the latter three are Bush_Common and Bush_Common_Flowers — the second is
; ALREADY imported and licence-cleared at assets/terrain/bush_common_flowers/ (gltf only, no
; .tscn wrapper yet). Unwired, not deleted, for PineTree as for DeadTree/PineTree2:
; PineTree.tscn stays on disk and test_pine_tree_import.gd still covers it, and
; quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres keeps its entry unchanged because that pack still
; supplies Rock/Rocks/Grass/Crops/Wheat elsewhere in the project.
; SINGLE-PACK AT LAST (2026-09-08, human ruling: "make sure all of our trees used the same
; Stylized Nature Megakit"). model_scenes is now 5 entries, ALL Stylized Nature MegaKit:
; CommonTree1 + CommonTree2 (round canopy, both already shipped and UNCHANGED), Pine1 (narrow
; conifer, NEW), TwistedTree1 (gnarled, NEW) and BushCommon (ground-level undergrowth, NEW
; wrapper over a mesh already imported for Scrub). Three distinct tree silhouettes plus
; undergrowth, all equal weight in pick_variant().
;
; WHY THE MEGAKIT AND NOT THE OTHERS: it is the pack that already supplies the GROUND these
; trees stand on — grass.tres, meadow.tres and wild_grass.tres all draw from it — and a tree
; sitting in grass is the adjacency that reads hardest. Forest had been drawing from three packs
; at once (MegaKit, Ultimate Nature Pack, Poly Pizza), more than any other terrain.
;
; RETIRED THIS PASS: BirchTree, Bush, BushBerries (all Ultimate Nature Pack) — the last
; non-MegaKit holdouts. Unwired, not deleted, the same disposition DeadTree/PineTree2/PineTree
; already have; their import suites still cover what the repo CONTAINS and are untouched.
;
; TWO LOSSES WITH NO MEGAKIT EQUIVALENT, both accepted by the human when the roster was chosen:
; there is NO birch mesh in the kit at any name, and NO berry bush — so BirchTree's white-trunk
; look and BushBerries' berry detail are simply gone rather than substituted. Undergrowth is one
; pick now (BushCommon) rather than two. Bush_Common_Flowers is deliberately NOT the second:
; `flowers` is Meadow's habitat tag and Meadow is its only source, so flowering shrubs stay off
; every other terrain (the same call scrub.tres already applies).
;
; PINE RESTORES A DELIBERATE LOSS. The conifer silhouette was added on 2026-08-16 to answer
; "every tree looks the same", then removed by this same day's earlier cull because it was the
; project's only Poly Pizza asset — that cull's note said the gap was RECOVERABLE, not closed.
; Pine1 is the recovery, from the audited pack. It is NOT the removed PineTree2, which came from
; the Textured Stylized Trees pack.
;
; 2 NEW IMPORTS, MegaKit, CC0 1.0, audit gate re-checked: Pine_1, TwistedTree_1. Bush_Common was
; already imported for Scrub and only gained a Forest wrapper here, at the SAME 0.37932 scale
; Scrub uses, so one mesh is never two heights in one world.
;
; ALL SCALES ARE MEASURED AGAINST THE ESTABLISHED ~2.5 TILE-UNIT CANOPY TARGET (Pine1 0.34168
; from raw height 7.316918; TwistedTree1 0.14948 from raw 16.7255 — a much larger source mesh,
; so the small factor is correct, not a typo). The TARGET itself remains a first-pass judgment
; call with no GDD number behind it — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF.
; PINE DROPPED, COMMONTREE3 IN ITS PLACE (2026-09-08, human eyeball pass on all five variants
; rendered side by side). The conifer slot is now a third round-canopy broadleaf.
;
; WHY, AND WHY IT IS NOT RECOVERABLE FROM THIS PACK: Pine1 rendered as a SOLID CONE — its
; foliage is `Leaf_Pine_C.png`, one flat frond silhouette, over 770 canopy triangles against
; CommonTree1's 1920 individually-cut leaves. All five kit pines share that texture, so none of
; them matches; Pine_4/Pine_5 are merely denser (1210/1158 tris), not different in kind. And the
; tall layered conifers in the pack's own Preview_4.jpg DO NOT SHIP HERE —
; `Leaves_GiantPine_C.png` is present in Textures/ but no GiantPine mesh exists in glTF, FBX or
; OBJ, because the free Standard set is 68 of 116 models. The preview advertises the PRO kit.
; The conifer silhouette is therefore UNAVAILABLE, not unchosen: re-adding one means buying PRO
; or putting a second pack back into Forest, which is what the standardisation removed.
; Pine1.tscn and its import stay on disk, unwired.
;
; THE RED PAIR WAS SPLIT (human ruling, 2026-09-08 second eyeball pass: "the Bush needs to be
; green not red. there is just too much red with this. The twisted tree being red is ok"). Both
; variants used to draw `Leaves_TwistedTree_C.png`, rgb(167,23,23) RED, kept as an autumn accent.
; Two of five reading as autumn was one too many, so BUSHCOMMON IS NOW GREEN and TwistedTree1 is
; the sole autumn accent.
;
; HOW THE BUSH WENT GREEN: the MegaKit ships Bush_Common.gltf pointing at the twisted tree's leaf
; atlas — that is the pack's own wiring, not an import slip. Every leaf texture in this kit is a
; FLAT SINGLE COLOUR plus an alpha cutout, so the recolour is exact and lossless: the bush's local
; copy is now `assets/terrain/bush_common/Leaves_Bush_C.png`, the identical 302938-pixel alpha mask
; with its RGB set to rgb(88,123,0) — the pack's OWN `Leaves_NormalTree_C` green, already worn by
; CommonTree1/2/3, so the bush is not a new colour value. The gltf's image + material names were
; renamed to match. TwistedTree1 keeps its own untouched red copy of the original texture.
;
; STILL DELIBERATE, DO NOT "FIX": TwistedTree1's RED leaves and its GREY `Bark_TwistedTree` trunk,
; where every other variant is brown. That half of the original ruling stands.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TerrainDefinition" load_steps=8 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/terrain_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/common_tree_1/CommonTree1.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://data/terrain/forest_harvest.tres" id="3_harvest"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/common_tree_2/CommonTree2.tscn" id="4_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/common_tree_3/CommonTree3.tscn" id="5_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/twisted_tree_1/TwistedTree1.tscn" id="6_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/bush_common/BushCommon.tscn" id="9_model"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "forest"
display_name = "Forest"
emitted_tags = Array[String](["forest"])
cost = 0
blocks_movement = true
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model"), ExtResource("4_model"), ExtResource("5_model"), ExtResource("6_model"), ExtResource("9_model")])
harvestable = ExtResource("3_harvest")
